.TH MEDIA 1 "October 2026" "scripts" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
media \- unified media lifecycle: C2PA attestation, invisible watermarking, Bitcoin timestamping & asset generation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B media
.RI <command> " [" options "] [" arguments "]"
.PP
.B Asset Pipeline:
.br
.B media init
.I name
.I version
.RB [ \-d " dir" ]
.RB [ \-p " proofs-dir" ]
.br
.B media build
.I name
.I version
.RB [ \-m " master" ]
.RB [ \-r " raw" ]
.RB [ \-d " dir" ]
.RB [ \-p " proofs-dir" ]
.RB [ \-\-sizes " sizes" ]
.RB [ \-\-bw " [" \fIitem\fR ]]
.RB [ \-\-no\-sign ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-stamp ]
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.br
.B media audit
.RI [ name ]
.RI [ version ]
.RB [ \-d " dir" ]
.RB [ \-p " proofs-dir" ]
.br
.B media list
.RB [ \-d " dir" ]
.RB [ \-p " proofs-dir" ]
.br
.B media upgrade
.RI [ target ]
.RI [ version ]
.RB [ \-d " dir" ]
.RB [ \-p " proofs-dir" ]
.PP
.B File Attestation:
.br
.B media sign
.I input
.RB [ \-o " output" ]
.RB [ \-\-in\-place ]
.RB [ \-\-stamp ]
.RB [ \-\-bw " [" \fIitem\fR ]]
.RB [ \-t " title" ]
.RB [ \-a " author" ]
.RB [ \-d " domain" ]
.RB [ \-w " watermark" ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-watermark ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-c2pa ]
.br
.B media verify
.I file
.RB [ \-\-ots " proof" ]
.RB [ \-\-bw " [" \fIitem\fR ]]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B media stamp
.I file
.RB [ \-f ]
.RB [ \-\-wait ]
.PP
.B Automation & Keys:
.br
.B media timer
.RB { setup " [" \fIdir\fR "] [" \-\-interval " \fIinterval\fR ]" | status | remove }
.br
.B media keys
.RB { show | gen " [" \-d " \fIdomain\fR ] [" \-\-bw " \fIitem\fR ]" | export | push " [" \fIitem\fR ] }
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBmedia\fR provides an end-to-end media attestation, provenance verification, asset packaging, and blockchain anchoring suite for the nada.mu ecosystem.
It integrates three independent cryptographic layers into a unified workflow:
.IP 1. 4
\fBC2PA Content Credentials\fR (Level 1 provenance manifest and X.509 claim signing).
.IP 2. 4
\fBDWT-DCT Steganography\fR (frequency-domain invisible watermarks resilient to crop, compression, and scaling).
.IP 3. 4
\fBOpenTimestamps\fR (cryptographic proof of existence anchored in the Bitcoin blockchain).
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Asset Pipeline
.TP
.B init \fIname\fR \fIversion\fR
Initializes the standardized directory hierarchy (\fB01_source/raw/\fR, \fB01_source/master/\fR, \fB02_signed/\fR, \fB03_dist/\fR, and the corresponding proofs directory) for a new asset version tag without building files.
.TP
.B build \fIname\fR \fIversion\fR
Constructs a complete versioned release from source materials. Automatically discovers existing master and raw files if already placed in \fB01_source/\fR, or scaffolds the structure if empty. Locks source files (\fBchmod 0444\fR), anchors sources in Bitcoin, produces the signed 1024px showcase release, generates downscaled distribution formats (WebP, PNG, and multi-layer \fBfavicon.ico\fR), and updates the atomic \fBlatest\fR symlink.
.TP
.B audit [\fIname\fR] [\fIversion\fR]
Executes a full non-blocking diagnostic pass across an asset version, an entire asset, or the whole library.
Collects and displays all integrity violations in a single unified report. Detects hash mismatches (content altered after timestamping), missing proofs (source files lacking \fI.ots\fR), corrupted proofs, and orphaned proofs.
.TP
.B list
Scans the managed icons library and lists all assets, available versions, active \fBlatest\fR pointers, and proofs archive locations.
.TP
.B upgrade [\fItarget\fR] [\fIversion\fR]
Recursively queries OpenTimestamps calendar servers to upgrade pending proofs into finalized Bitcoin block header attestations.
Can target an individual file, directory, specific asset version (\fBmedia upgrade duck v1\fR), or the entire proofs library.
.SS File Attestation
.TP
.B sign \fIinput\fR
Signs an arbitrary image (PNG, JPG, WebP, AVIF, SVG, TIFF) with C2PA Content Credentials and embeds an invisible frequency-domain watermark. With \fB\-\-stamp\fR, also anchors the file in the Bitcoin blockchain.
.TP
.B verify \fIfile\fR
Inspects and verifies all three attestation layers of a media file: C2PA manifest validity, DWT-DCT invisible watermark extraction, and OpenTimestamps Bitcoin blockchain confirmation status.
.TP
.B stamp \fIfile\fR
Anchors any file in the Bitcoin blockchain via OpenTimestamps, producing a detached \fI.ots\fR proof file.
.SS Automation & Timers
.TP
.B timer setup [\fIdir\fR] [\-\-interval \fI2h\fR]
Configures, enables, and starts a systemd user timer (\fBmedia-ots.timer\fR) that periodically scans the specified proofs folder and upgrades pending Bitcoin timestamp proofs. Defaults to \fB~/Seafile/Icons-Proofs\fR.
.TP
.B timer status
Displays the active status, triggers, and execution history of the background systemd upgrade timer.
.TP
.B timer remove
Disables and removes the background systemd timer and service units.
.SS Keys & Vault
.TP
.B keys show
Displays the active C2PA certificate information, issuer, validity period, and credential storage location (Bitwarden or local disk).
.TP
.B keys gen [\-d \fIdomain\fR] [\-\-bw \fIitem\fR]
Generates a new ECDSA P-256 Root CA and Leaf End-Entity signing certificate chain. Can write to disk or directly into Bitwarden vault.
.TP
.B keys export
Prints raw PEM blocks of the private key and certificate chain to standard output for secure backups.
.TP
.B keys push [\fIitem\fR]
Uploads local signing keys directly into Bitwarden vault as a Secure Note and sets it as the default vault item.
.TP
.B keys use [\fIitem\fR]
Configures the default Bitwarden vault item to load signing credentials from (pass \fIlocal\fR to revert to disk).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-m ", " \-\-master " file"
Path to normalized square master image (PNG, WebP). Auto-detected if present in \fB01_source/master/\fR.
.TP
.BI \-r ", " \-\-raw " file"
Path to original project canvas (\fI.xcf\fR, \fI.psd\fR, \fI.svg\fR). Auto-detected if present in \fB01_source/raw/\fR.
.TP
.BI \-d ", " \-\-dir " path"
Base directory for the managed icons library (default: current directory if named \fIIcons\fR, \fB$SEAFILE_ICONS\fR, \fI~/Seafile/Icons\fR, \fB$SEADRIVE_ICONS\fR, or \fI~/SeaDrive/My Libraries/Icons\fR).
.TP
.BI \-p ", " \-\-proofs\-dir " path"
Base directory for the separated OpenTimestamps proofs archive (default: sibling \fI<icons>-Proofs\fR, \fB$SEAFILE_PROOFS\fR, \fI~/Seafile/Icons\-Proofs\fR, \fB$SEADRIVE_PROOFS\fR, or \fI~/SeaDrive/My Libraries/Icons\-Proofs\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-sizes " list"
Comma-separated list of target resolutions for dist rendering (default: \fB512,256,128,64,32\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-bw ", " \-\-bw\-item " item"
Retrieves C2PA signing private key and certificate chain directly from Bitwarden into RAM (0 disk writes). Default item: \fBc2pa-signer\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-no\-sign
Bypasses C2PA manifest signing and steganographic watermarking.
.TP
.BI \-\-no\-stamp
Bypasses OpenTimestamps blockchain anchoring.
.TP
.BI \-\-force
Forces re-building and re-stamping even if pre-flight audit reports mismatches.
.TP
.BI \-\-json
Outputs raw structured inspection data in JSON format for scripting.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SEAFILE_ICONS
Overrides default base directory for icons library.
.TP
.B SEAFILE_PROOFS
Overrides default base directory for proofs archive.
.TP
.B BW_SESSION
Bitwarden vault session token used for in-memory credential loading.
.TP
.B C2PA_PRIVATE_KEY
Raw PEM private key passed via environment.
.TP
.B C2PA_CERT
Raw PEM certificate chain passed via environment.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.B Build new icon version from sources:
.RS
.nf
media init duck v1
# (place duck.xcf in 01_source/raw/ and duck_crop.png in 01_source/master/)
media build duck v1 --bw
media audit duck v1
.fi
.RE
.PP
.B Sign individual image with Bitwarden keys and Bitcoin timestamp:
.RS
.nf
media sign --bw --stamp hero_banner.png
media verify hero_banner_signed.png
.fi
.RE
.PP
.B Configure automated Bitcoin proof upgrade timer on remote server:
.RS
.nf
media timer setup /home/apps/data/Icons-Proofs --interval 2h
media timer status
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ots (1),
.BR seaf-cli (1)
